lay areas improving shop  Frontage improving public realm Works  improving uh Village halls and Community  facilities we really want to demonstrate  the residents that they can see visible  improvements for this funding so you can  find out more about that on our website  and and we'll hopefully be successful in  the in the funding application uh in  October and then we'll start we're  already starting to uh to to progress  the different ways in which we want to  spend that that important funding and  then also we've recently back in the  earlier part of the summer we applied  for over 17 million pounds to elevate  eckington so that was our bid as part of  the leveling up on the government's  leveling up for and that would be some  major town center regeneration in  eckington complete redesign of the town  center and improvements as well as a  sort of super Park if you like at  Lansbury Road play area so we we haven't  found out yet whether that's been  successful but we don't necessarily know  whether we will be or not but in any  case all of the work that we've done to  prepare that bid means that in future if  we're not successful this time we can  keep applying and making sure that we  get that vital funding to help really  improve efforts and Town Center which I  know has been on a lot of people's minds  in epoxy for a long time now over in  dronfield sports center we recently ran  together with a DWP a job spare to help  local people find local jobs in the drum  field area really thanks to everyone who  came to exhibit and show their  organizations off and to all the  prospective job Hunters who came I  really hope that was useful it's a key  commitment for us as an Administration  to hold regular jobs Affairs to help  local people find local jobs so I'm  really really pleased to do that I'm  sure there'll be more coming up to stay  tuned to our website and our social  media to find out about other job  players we'll be doing if you're looking  for a job yourself so this past month  we've been supporting organic September  which is a fantastic scheme which helps  encourage people to be more organic in  their in their shopping choices and  helps you know promote a better  environment and and helps to deal with  some of the issues around climate change  there's loads more information on our on  our website around how you can shop more  organically in terms of clothes and food  and all those sorts of things so please  do check out our website for more  information on that one now you may also  have been following recently in the  local media that our area so at  Derbyshire and Derby City and  Nottinghamshire and Nottingham City has  been successful in securing a Devolution  deal from the government now this is a  30-year deal with the government that's  worth a total of 1.14 billion for our  region and there's various other funding  mechanisms and schemes that would go  with that to support things like  Brownfield housing and things like  climate change and all those sorts of  things in theory and looking at it at  face value it looks like good news for  our region it you know in East Midlands  has long have been underserved in terms  of investment in infrastructure and  education and those sorts of things so  in theory it should be good the one key  challenge is that the in order to access  that deal the area the region is  required to have an elected mayor now  that doesn't change anything in terms of  how the councils are run you will still  have a district council as well  Northeast average District Council  you'll still have Derbyshire County  Council doing the same things that we  already already do the mayor would have  powers handed down from government to to  to to deal with things on a sort of  regional level if you like within our  region and I know views really vary on  on elected Mayors and I you know I'm not  I'm not the biggest fan myself but I  recognize that actually in order to  access that really important investment  in our region it may be the sacrifice  that we have to make you'll be hearing  more and more about this over time  there'll be consultation with residents  and and you'll be able to find out a bit  more about it but that's just to give  you the heads up and stay tuned for more  updates on that moving forward finally  just just want to say please do come  down and have a look at kilimash active  are almost brand new Leisure Center here  in killer Marsh when it's when it's open  we'll really look forward to welcoming  you and hopefully we can sign you up for  a membership uh and have a go on the  spin studio or the or the gym or even  just go and bring the kids and go on the  soft play area it really is a fantastic  facility and we're really looking  forward to showing it off to Not Just  Killer Marsh residents but residents  from across the whole District I'll look  forward to seeing you next month until  then just to say stay tuned to our  website and our social media channel for  more updates as they happen we look  forward to seeing you next month  foreign
 

